 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## Cache Replacement (2Q)
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a completed preview sheet is admitted to the preview worker's cache, the system SHALL insert the entry at the MRU end of the A1 recency queue (the FIFO queue holding first-use sheets).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a cache hit occurs on an entry in the A1 recency queue, the system SHALL remove the entry from A1 and insert it at the MRU end of the A2 reused queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a cache hit occurs on an entry in the A2 reused queue, the system SHALL move the entry to the MRU end of A2.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When the A1 recency queue holds more than one quarter of the cache's entry capacity, the system SHALL evict A1's LRU entry and discard its cached JPEG data entirely (such an entry has had no second access).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When eviction is required for admission and A1 is within its entry-capacity bound, the system SHALL evict A2's LRU entry.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When any eviction is required, the system SHALL evict before admission so total cached JPEG data remains within 12 GiB.
